<title>USA: AMR Corp Q3 net rose.</title>
<headline>AMR Corp Q3 net rose.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $3.06		    $2.96</p>
<p> Shr diluted		$3.06		    $2.64</p>
<p> Net			282,000		  229,000</p>
<p> Revs		   4,562,000		4,445,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  92,000		   77,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted	92,000		   91,000</p>
<p>		     Nine Months</p>
<p> Shr			  $8.53		    $5.77</p>
<p> Shr diluted		$8.11		    $5.26</p>
<p> Net			732,000		  444,000</p>
<p> Revs		  13,420,000	    12,7722,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  86,000		   77,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted	92,000		   91,000</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q3 net includes pretax costs of $21 million for company's share of travel agency litigation settlement.</p>
<p>1995 net includes after tax extraordinary charges of $4 million in quarter and $17 million in nine months. These had per share impact of $0.05 and $0.23, respectively, primary and $0.04 and $0.19 fully diluted. -- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
